{#- PatchMon server: one Go binary (API + embedded UI, runs its own DB
   migrations on start) plus postgres and valkey, on a private docker
   network (`network`). Only the server publishes a port. Upstream
   docker/docker-compose.yml, except: valkey instead of redis (drop-in, the
   same image netbox uses) without a password (no published port, nothing
   else on the network), and no guacd sidecar (in-browser RDP — not used,
   and the agents' ssh/rdp proxies stay off anyway).

   All server state lives in postgres; the server container has no volume.

   http_port: host port (container listens on 3000 — forgejo has 3000
   itself). cors_origin must be the URL the browser uses.

   Secrets (OpenBao via pillar): jwt_secret, session_secret,
   ai_encryption_key (`openssl rand -hex 64` each), db_password. Written to
   files in secrets_dir (0700 root) — the server's env file (it loads
   ENV_FILE itself, incl. DATABASE_URL) and postgres' POSTGRES_PASSWORD_FILE
   — each bound read-only into its container. So never in the container
   env, state diffs or `docker inspect`. The files are 0444 because the
   images' users are unknown/vary; the 0700 dir keeps host users out. All
   four required: the formula fails on a blank or unresolved one.

   dump_dir: target of formulas/backup's pre-run pg_dump (pillar/backup.sls
   `dumps` repeats the path and postgres_container_name — change both). #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'image': 'ghcr.io/patchmon/patchmon-server',
    'tag': '2.1.8',
    'postgres_image': 'docker.io/library/postgres',
    'postgres_tag': '17.11-alpine',
    'valkey_image': 'docker.io/valkey/valkey',
    'valkey_tag': '9.1.3-alpine',
    'container_name': 'patchmon',
    'postgres_container_name': 'patchmon-postgres',
    'valkey_container_name': 'patchmon-valkey',
    'network': 'patchmon',
    'http_port': 3001,
    'cors_origin': '',
    'base_dir': '/opt/patchmon',
    'postgres_dir': '/opt/patchmon/postgres',
    'valkey_dir': '/opt/patchmon/valkey',
    'dump_dir': '/opt/patchmon/dump',
    'secrets_dir': '/opt/patchmon/secrets',
    'db_name': 'patchmon_db',
    'db_user': 'patchmon_user',
    'timezone': 'Etc/UTC',
    'jwt_secret': '',
    'session_secret': '',
    'ai_encryption_key': '',
    'db_password': '',
    'env': {},
} %}
{%- set patchmon = salt['pillar.get']('patchmon:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
